You already understand our current OneOps file-watcher setup. We are replacing that file watcher.Context and decisions already made
We are replacing the existing OneOps file-watcher detection and readiness logic.
Phase 1 scope is SFTP only. Kafka is a future source-adapter seam only (no Kafka runtime in this phase).
The new watcher must be fully config-driven from OneRec feed metadata (no feed-specific hard-coding).
The watcher owns detection, completeness checking, claiming, idempotency, and emission of a readiness signal.
The actual file loading stays with the existing OneOps loader for now, provided it can accept an external readiness signal (this is still an open question).
We are in discovery. We do not have the OneOps codebase. Everything is a working baseline until confirmed with SMEs.
Delivery assumption: 3 dedicated FTEs, roughly 12–14 weeks if key interfaces are confirmed early.
Reconciliation-critical concerns: completeness before ready, correct COB / late-file handling, idempotency, and durable audit.
